# Admin event info

When the user asks to **admin / add / update / insert / fix event info**, do not half-fill cards. Research official sources and write a complete, catalog-consistent row (or batch). Prefer official festival/tour/venue/presenter pages over resale or wiki alone.

## Always resolve

| Field | Expectation |
|--------|-------------|
| `name` | Match catalog patterns below; reuse existing spelling for the same brand/tour |
| `date` | Correct local calendar day (timestamptz date portion) |
| `city` | `City, XX` per city-format rule |
| `location` | Venue / site name as billed |
| `season` | From date (`Winter`/`Spring`/`Summer`/`Fall` + year) |
| `show_type` | Usually `music` for concerts/fests |
| `featured_artists` | Headliner(s) for shows/tours. Festivals: see **Artist-triggered festivals**. Catalog spelling |
| `header_tags` | Genres + `Festival` on festival cards (genres alone is not enough) |
| `producers` | Only with explicit presenter credit (producers-accuracy) |
| `countdown_link` | **Future events only.** If the event date is still ahead, set official tickets / event page (artist Ticketmaster hub, fest site, venue). Not StubHub/SeatGeek unless nothing else exists. If the event is already past, leave `countdown_link` null / empty (do not backfill ticket links onto past shows). The app clears the link automatically when the countdown pill hits zero (`clear_expired_countdown_link`) and via a daily DB sweep. |
| `image_url` | Must be a **Cloudflare R2 public CDN URL** (`https://images.secretblogger.app/event/…`). Source may be an external promo/press link, but always rehost via `ingest-event-image` / `ensureEventImageStored` (or `scripts/backfill-event-images.mjs`) before saving. Never leave hotlinks, and never write `*.supabase.co/storage/…` URLs. |
| `custom_tags` | All billed openers / special guests / supporting acts as `special-guests` (see below) |
| `created_by` | Admin `9ab4f944-acce-463b-8f0d-a1a12b52a24c` on inserts |

Also set `formatted_address` when you can resolve a stable venue address.

## Shows and tours: support billing

When adding a **headline show or tour night**, research support for **that date** (tour announce, Ticketmaster/venue page, official artist site):

1. Put the headliner(s) in `featured_artists`.
2. Put **every billed** special guest, opener, and supporting act in `custom_tags.special-guests` (array). Do not skip “also appearing” / “with…” / regional openers when the source lists them for that night.
3. If support differs by market/leg, set guests **per night**, not one tour-wide guess.
4. If a night truly has no announced support, leave `special-guests` empty. If support is rumored but not billed, omit it.
5. Catalog spelling for guest names (artist-name-spelling).
6. **Full tour, not one night.** If you add or update **any** date of a named tour (or clearly announced tour leg), also add/update **every other public headline night** on that same tour / leg from the official announce or Ticketmaster hub. Do not leave a lone market because that was the only city the user named. Skip private / TV / festival slots per usual fest rules; for festivals on the routing, take the full fest run (see below) or skip the fest entirely.

## Artist-triggered festivals

When the user asks to admin an **artist** and that leads to adding or updating a **festival** card (Pride, OUTLOUD, LadyLand, Homobloc, Coachella day, etc.):

1. Do **not** insert a fest card that only lists that artist (or a short cherry-picked subset).
2. Research the **official full lineup for that day/card** from the fest site, presenter, or a complete set-times source.
3. Put **every announced act** for that day into `featured_artists` (expand billed B2Bs into the named DJs/acts; keep catalog spelling).
4. If the full day bill is unclear, incomplete, or only “and more…”, **skip that fest card** (or ask) until it is clear. Prefer skipping over a partial ship.
5. Multi-day fests: one card per day with that day’s complete bill, not one blended weekend list.
6. **Full run, not one day.** If you add or update **any** day of a multi-day festival edition, also add/update **every other day** of that same run (same fest + edition year) when those days exist. Do not leave a lone Day 2 because the tracked artist only played that day. Apply the same full-lineup bar to each sibling day; if any day cannot be completed, skip or ask for the whole run rather than shipping a partial weekend.

## Naming

- Tours: `Artist: Tour Name` (colon separator; no em dash / hyphen title splits)
- Recurring festivals: include edition year (`Coachella '26:…`, `Beyond the Valley '25: Day 1`, `Wildlands Brisbane '26`)
- One-off shows: no year in the title unless the official name includes it
- Multi-day fests: `…: Day N` (or Coachella `Weekend N: Weekday` when that is official)
- Same edition = same year token on every day of that run (NYE fests use the marketed edition year, e.g. Dec 2025–Jan 2026 → `'25`)

## Consistency checks

1. Query existing rows for the same artist/fest/tour before insert; mirror producers, genres, link, image, and title shape.
2. Artist / producer / guest strings: catalog spelling (artist-name-spelling).
3. After a batch: re-check for duplicate spellings, missing `Festival` on fest cards, and bare recurring titles that collide across years.
4. If unsure on producers or a fact, leave null / ask; do not invent.

## Images

- **Host on the Cloudflare R2 image CDN only.** External URLs are source material for ingest, never the stored `image_url`. Use `ensureEventImageStored` / `ingest-event-image`, or `node scripts/backfill-event-images.mjs` after a SQL batch.
- Do **not** upload event photos to Supabase Storage. That path is what blew cached egress on the free plan.
- Uploads must set `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable` and use a new UUID path (never overwrite).
- Feed cards load the sibling `.card.jpg` (640px). Keep `image_url` on the full object for OG/share.
- Must be wider than tall (card-friendly landscape). Reject square/vertical-only assets when a horizontal exists.
- Must be connected to the event: that festival’s grounds/crowd/stage, that tour’s official promo, or that night’s billed art. Not a random artist headshot, Unsplash crowd, or decade-old Wikimedia of a different year.
- Festivals: prefer recent press from **that** fest. Tours: official tour poster / press still used for that run.

## Do not

- Ship festival days with only genre tags and no `Festival`
- Add a festival just because the tracked artist played it, with only that artist (or a partial lineup) on the card
- Add only the fest day the tracked artist played and leave the other days of that edition missing
- Add only one (or a few) nights of a named tour / tour leg and leave the rest of that announce missing
- Ship a festival card with a partial/guessed lineup when the official day bill is incomplete or unavailable
- Ship a headline show with announced openers/special guests missing from `special-guests`
- Reuse one tour image for an unrelated festival day (or the reverse) without a reason
- Leave `countdown_link` empty on a **future** event when an official URL is findable in a normal search
- Add or keep a `countdown_link` on a **past** event (clear it when touching past rows if it’s still set)
- Use vertical posters, generic stock, or old photos from a different edition when a current horizontal promo exists
- Write hotlinked `image_url` values straight into the DB and skip rehost
- Write `image_url` to Supabase Storage (`/storage/v1/object/public/`)
